WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.544 --> 00:00:16.617
"Ahoy, mateys!" Miss Shelly called.

2
00:00:16.618 --> 00:00:19.767
It was Talk Like a Pirate Day at Kids Central.

3
00:00:19.768 --> 00:00:22.204
Everyone was dressed up.

4
00:00:22.205 --> 00:00:27.162
"Yo, ho, ho!" Nina wore a purple eye patch.

5
00:00:27.163 --> 00:00:31.315
Bobby had made his cast look like a peg leg.

6
00:00:31.316 --> 00:00:35.516
"Hey, Ethan, what's on your shoulder?" he asked.

7
00:00:35.517 --> 00:00:39.317
"A parrot, of course!" Ethan replied.

8
00:00:39.318 --> 00:00:41.808
Jason waved a rubber sword.

9
00:00:41.809 --> 00:00:44.896
"Shiver me timbers!"

10
00:00:44.897 --> 00:00:48.633
"I hope you pirates are hungry," Miss Shelly said.

11
00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:52.528
"We're having a pirate feast."

12
00:00:52.529 --> 00:00:56.350
"What are we making?" Nina asked.

13
00:00:56.351 --> 00:01:01.540
"Pirate peg legs and sea sauce," Miss Shelly said.

14
00:01:01.541 --> 00:01:06.720
"I hope we're not eating my peg leg!" Bobby said.

15
00:01:06.721 --> 00:01:09.711
Miss Shelly laughed.

16
00:01:09.712 --> 00:01:15.044
"Don't worry. We're making fish sticks with tartar sauce."

17
00:01:15.045 --> 00:01:19.258
She looked around. "Where's Izzie?"

18
00:01:19.259 --> 00:01:24.130
"Here." Izzie entered the gym and sat down.

19
00:01:24.131 --> 00:01:25.880
She didn't look happy.

20
00:01:25.881 --> 00:01:28.385
And she wasn't dressed like a pirate.

21
00:01:28.386 --> 00:01:31.254
"What's up, Izzie?" Jason asked.

22
00:01:31.255 --> 00:01:35.499
"I don't want to be a pirate," Izzie said.

23
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.957
"You don't have to be a pirate," Miss Shelly said.

24
00:01:38.958 --> 00:01:42.609
"But everyone has to help with making our snack.

25
00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:46.406
We'll make the pirate peg legs first."

26
00:01:46.407 --> 00:01:51.804
"I'll preheat the oven!" Jason said.

27
00:01:51.805 --> 00:01:55.197
Nina followed the directions on the board.

28
00:01:55.198 --> 00:01:59.262
"First, we beat two eggs.

29
00:01:59.263 --> 00:02:05.857
Then, we pour bread crumbs into a shallow bowl."

30
00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:10.975
"Next, we dip the pieces of fish in the eggs," Jason read.

31
00:02:10.976 --> 00:02:14.808
"Then into the bread crumbs," Bobby added.

32
00:02:14.809 --> 00:02:19.468
"Remember to use a fork for dipping," Miss Shelly said.

33
00:02:19.469 --> 00:02:25.740
The kids took turns dipping the fish into the eggs and bread crumbs.

34
00:02:25.741 --> 00:02:33.236
"Now we put the fish on a tray," Bobby said.

35
00:02:33.237 --> 00:02:39.422
Jason carefully slid the tray into the toaster oven.

36
00:02:39.423 --> 00:02:42.452
Izzie sat at a table, still looking glum.

37
00:02:42.453 --> 00:02:44.571
Miss Shelly went over.

38
00:02:44.572 --> 00:02:46.887
"What's bothering you, Izzie?"

39
00:02:46.888 --> 00:02:51.345
"I don't like Talk Like a Pirate Day," Izzie said.

40
00:02:51.346 --> 00:02:55.062
"I don't want to talk like a boy."

41
00:02:55.063 --> 00:02:59.138
"There were female pirates too," Miss Shelly said.

42
00:02:59.139 --> 00:03:01.849
"No way," Jason said.

43
00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:06.783
"The pirates in my video game say girls are bad luck on a ship!"

44
00:03:06.784 --> 00:03:10.844
"Well, they never met Anne Bonny and Mary Read."

45
00:03:10.845 --> 00:03:13.362
Miss Shelly handed Izzie a book.

46
00:03:13.363 --> 00:03:18.086
"These women are two of history's fiercest pirates."

47
00:03:18.087 --> 00:03:24.181
"Really?" Izzie grinned. "Cool!"

48
00:03:24.182 --> 00:03:26.885
Nina took off her purple eye patch.

49
00:03:26.886 --> 00:03:29.771
"Do you want to wear my eye patch, Izzie?"

50
00:03:29.772 --> 00:03:35.119
"Aye!" Izzie laughed.

51
00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:39.811
"Thanks, Nina. Can we make the sea sauce now?"

52
00:03:39.812 --> 00:03:41.433
Miss Shelly nodded.

53
00:03:41.434 --> 00:03:46.029
"Let's turn the fish sticks first."

54
00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.920
The kids started making the sauce.

55
00:03:48.921 --> 00:03:54.188
"We add one cup of mayonnaise to a medium bowl," Bobby read.

56
00:03:54.189 --> 00:04:00.385
"Now we need six tablespoons of chopped sweet pickles," Jason said.

57
00:04:00.386 --> 00:04:04.268
"Squeeze one lemon for juice," Ethan said.

58
00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:07.596
"Then mix!" Izzie said.

59
00:04:07.597 --> 00:04:14.970
The kids took turns measuring, squeezing, and mixing.

60
00:04:14.971 --> 00:04:21.281
Ding! The timer rang.

61
00:04:21.282 --> 00:04:26.353
"Yay! Our pirate peg legs are ready!" Bobby said.

62
00:04:26.354 --> 00:04:29.219
Everyone sat down.

63
00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:32.501
Izzie raised her water bottle to make a toast.

64
00:04:32.502 --> 00:04:40.937
"These peg legs look delicious. Eat up, pirates!"
